    "title": "<p><strong>Table 9.03</strong>&nbsp;Histological characteristics and molecular phenotype of breast cancer in <em>BRCA1</em> and <em>BRCA2</em> mutation carriers compared with sporadic breast cancer</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Source: Modified from 21336636, van der Groep P, van der Wall E, van Diest PJ: Pathology of hereditary breast cancer. Cellular oncology 2011, 34:71-88.",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"width: 456.7pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Characteristic(s)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 348.5pt; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: none; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"465\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong>Typical findings in mutation carriers</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; border: none; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>BRCA1</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><em>BRCA2</em></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Clinical</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">More lung and brain metastases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">More bone and soft tissue metastases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Margin</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Well demarcated, solid nests, no tubule formation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">More often pushing borders</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Lymphocytic infiltrate</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Prominent lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Less lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate than in <em>BRCA1</em> carriers, but more than in sporadic cancer</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Necrosis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Often necrosis, fibrotic focus</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">May be present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Lymphovascular invasion</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Often present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Less common</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Grade</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">High histological grade</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Variable histological grade (mainly grade&nbsp;2 or 3)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Histological types</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">IBC, IBC with medullary pattern, metaplastic</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">IBC-NST, tubular, cribriform, mucinous, classic/pleomorphic lobular</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>In situ cancer</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Little DCIS</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">More frequently present with DCIS alone</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Little LCIS</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">LCIS may be present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Immunophenotype</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">ER/PR&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">ER/PR+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">ERBB2 (HER2)&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">ERBB2 (HER2)&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">High MIB1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Variable MIB1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Molecular type</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Triple-negative: ER&minus;, PR&minus;, ERBB2 (HER2)&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Luminal&nbsp;A: ER+, PR+, ERBB2 (HER2)&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Basal-like: CK5/6+, CK14+ or EGFR (HER1)+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CK5/6&minus;/CK14&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Gene expression</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Genes involved in proliferation, adhesion, angiogenesis, motility, transcription, DNA repair</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Genes involved in proliferation, adhesion, signal transduction, extracellular matrix production</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CK8/18&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CK8/18+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">EGFR (HER1)+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">EGFR (HER1)+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">p53+, very often <em>TP53</em> mutations</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">p53+/&minus;, ~50% <em>TP53</em> mutations</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cyclin&nbsp;D1&minus;, cyclin&nbsp;A and cyclin&nbsp;E high</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cyclin&nbsp;D1+, cyclin&nbsp;A and cyclin&nbsp;E variable</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">BCL2 low</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">BCL2 high</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">HIF1&alpha;+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">FGF1+, FGFR1+, FGFR2+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 108.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"144\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">p63+, P-cadherin+, caveolin-1+, vimentin+, laminin+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 174.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"232\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">DCIS, ductal carcinoma in situ; IBC, invasive breast carcinoma; LCIS, lobular carcinoma in situ; NST, of no special type.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Based on data from {<span class=\"highlight\">21336636}.</span></p>",
